==English==
===Etymology===
From {{suffix|sad|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈsadli/}}
*{{audio|en-us-sadly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[sad]] manner; [[sorrowfully]].
# [[unfortunately|Unfortunately]], [[sad to say]].
#:''If you think you’re getting out of this place alive, you are '''sadly''' mistaken, my friend.''
#:'''''Sadly''', the two were never to meet again.''
# {{obsolete}} [[deeply|Deeply]], [[completely]].
#* '''1485''', [[w:Thomas Malory|Sir Thomas Malory]], ''Le Morte Darthur'', Book VI:
#*: and there he founde a bed, and layde hym therein, and felle on slepe '''sadly'''.

====Usage notes====
In sense of “unfortunately”, most often used either in the collocation “sadly mistaken” or as a {{w|sentence adverb}}. See discussion of sentence modifiers at {{term|hopefully#Usage notes|hopefully}} and {{term|regretfully#Usage notes|regretfully}}.

===Synonyms===
* {{sense|in a sad manner}} {{l|en|sorrowfully}}, {{l|en|ruefully}}, {{l|en|mournfully}}, {{l|en|regretfully}} {{qualifier|various terms for particular shades of sadness}}
* {{sense|unfortunately}} {{l|en|unfortunately}}, {{l|en|sad to say}}, {{l|en|regrettably}}, {{l|en|regretfully}}, {{l|en|alas}}

